  "final_message": "I wrote the answer to `answer.json`:\n\n```json\n{\"delays_seconds\": [60, 120, 240, 480], \"total_attempts\": 5, \"final_status\": \"failed\"}\n```\n\nI got this by reading `billing/webhooks.py`, not by running the code.\n\n- **Delays:** After a failed attempt, the next one is scheduled `60 * 2^(attempts-1)` seconds later. That gives 60, 120, 240 and 480 seconds after attempts 1 to 4.\n- **Timing:** Delivery runs every second and skips a delivery until its scheduled time, so each retry fires at the scheduled time. A 500 is never a success, so every attempt fails.\n- **Attempts and status:** `MAX_ATTEMPTS` is 5. On the 5th failure the delivery is marked `failed` and no further retry is scheduled.\n\nI didn't run the tests, and I changed no files other than `answer.json`.",
